  "basis": "The chart shows Store B monthly sales in $K for April, May, and June. The April bar's top aligns with the y-axis tick 250 and the red dashed horizontal line labeled 'Average' (located at the April x-axis label, plot area/y-axis, and right side of the dashed line). May is 450 and June is 350, so April is the lowest of the three but exactly at the displayed average. The task state provides no policy table, threshold, or rule defining 'low-sales' or 'strong-sales' (policy_tables is empty and page_instructions contain no numerical triggers). Because the April value is at the average benchmark rather than below it, and no rule maps 'average' to a low-sales response, the low-sales route is not supported. The strong-sales route is also not supported because April is not above the average. With no specified trigger for low or strong sales, the only route consistent with the observed average-level value and the absence of a deviation trigger is normal monitoring.",
  "option_label": "Keep April on normal sales monitoring"
}
